# A World's place with a bundle answer whose parts are all `ignore`, whose constant field
# reads a building `if`'s late plain result written below it (Semantics ch. 4, "Binding
# groups and cycles": any line may use any name the block binds, and the order of a
# group's lines decides positions and nothing else; ch. 8, "A new place's first value";
# Type System ch. 2, "Bundles and sparse tuples": `ignore` takes a part and binds
# nothing). With a named part the program lowers
# (conformance/sem-ch04-late-value-above-in-bundle-place-field). Reaches `BindLate`'s
# marker "the late result `n` read at its block's build" on prismc-fd1.
# Written by Claude (sweep-7, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.* | Pad.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

tag Pad.Port of Element ((Nat, $Text)):
    name: Text

@Page: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Page loud:
    ((ignore, ignore)) <- Pad.Port(name="port {n}")                    # 0
    Ui.Label($text=$"of {n}")                                          # 1
    n <- if loud:
        Ui.Label($text=$"loud")                                        # 2
        @ 10
    else:
        @ 20
